{"case_id":"T5014","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","input_semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["plist_new_unix_date","plist_get_unix_date_val","plist_set_unix_date_val","plist_unix_date_val_compare","PList::Date::Date","PList::Date::SetValue","PList::Date::GetValue","datetime_to_timestamp","timestamp_to_datetime"],"reason":"H0 only passes raw bytes to plist_from_bin, plist_from_json, plist_from_openstep, or plist_from_xml and then calls plist_free. It never directly exercises the new UNIX-date API or performs create/set/get/compare operation sequences. Consequently, fuzz-controlled int64_t boundary timestamps, PLIST_DATE versus wrong-type nodes, and the conversions among int64_t, double, time_t, and the MAC_EPOCH offset are materially uncovered.","evidence":["plist_new_unix_date stores `(double)sec - MAC_EPOCH`, while plist_set_unix_date_val stores `(double)(sec - MAC_EPOCH)`, exposing distinct boundary arithmetic semantics.","plist_get_unix_date_val converts the stored double with `(int64_t)val + MAC_EPOCH`, but none of the four H0 targets invokes this getter on parsed or constructed PLIST_DATE nodes.","plist_unix_date_val_compare calls plist_get_unix_date_val and has a separate non-PLIST_DATE branch, neither of which H0 exercises.","Date::Date(int64_t), Date::SetValue(int64_t), and Date::GetValue() route through the new C API, whereas H0 never instantiates the C++ Date interface.","datetime_to_timestamp and timestamp_to_datetime introduce PyObject, time_t, mktime, and gmtime conversion paths absent from H0."],"recommended_action":"Add a structured date/API fuzz target that derives int64_t timestamps and operation choices from the input, exercises plist_new_unix_date, plist_set_unix_date_val, plist_get_unix_date_val, and plist_unix_date_val_compare on date and non-date nodes, and checks create/set/get/compare plus parse/serialize round trips at INT64_MIN, INT64_MAX, MAC_EPOCH boundaries, negative timestamps, and double-precision transition values. Add a Python-aware target for datetime_to_timestamp and timestamp_to_datetime if the Cython bridge is shipped."}
